     - Haemoglobin S/normal (heterozygous for haemoglobin S): This results in sickle cell heterozygotes, which are not affected but can transmit the disease.  
     - Normal/β-thalthaassaea (heterozygous for β-thalthaasaea): This results in β-thalthaassaea heterozygotes, which are usually well tolerated but may have mild symptoms.  
