The relationship between vapor pressure and PEL is that higher vapor pressures generally correspond to lower PEL values. This is because higher vapor pressures mean that the substance can evaporate more easily, leading to higher concentrations in the air. To maintain safe exposure levels, the PEL values are set to account for the ease with which a substance can evaporate and potentially reach dangerous concentrations.

