Given that the standard enthalpy of combustion of propane is -2220 kJ/mol and we have 2.5 moles of propane, we can plug these values into the equation:

q = 2.5 moles × (-2220 kJ/mol)

q = -5550 kJ

Therefore, the amount of heat released when 2.5 moles of propane is completely burned in oxygen gas is -5550 kJ.
