","The molecular formula C4H10O suggests that there are possible isomers of the alcohol (R-OH) functional group. In this case, the possible types of isomerism are chain isomerism and optical isomerism.

1. Chain isomerism: This type of isomerism occurs when the carbon atoms are arranged in different ways in the chain. For C4H10O, there are two possible chain isomers:

   a. Butan-1-ol (straight chain): CH3-CH2-CH2-CH2-OH
