- **Statement-2** is false because the flux depends on the area of the surface. The flux \( \oint \mathbf{F} \cdot d\mathbf{A} \) is the integral of the field over the surface. If the field is \( 1/r^2 \), the flux through a larger surface will be greater than that through a smaller surface, even if the source is the same. 

