- \(G = 26 \times 10^9\) N m\(^{-2}\)
- \(b = 0.286 \times 10^{-9}\) m
- \(d = 6 \times 10^{-8}\) m

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{26 \times 10^9 \times 0.286 \times 10^{-9}}{6 \times 10^{-8}}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{7.416 \times 10^2}{6 \times 10^{-8}}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = 1.236 \times 10^{10} \text{ N m}^{-2}
\]

Thus, the contribution of these particles to the tensile yield strength is \(\boxed{1.236 \times 10^9 \text{ N m}^{-2}}\).

