","To calculate the change in total entropy, we sum the change in entropy for the gases and the water separately.

1. **Change in entropy of the gases**:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{gases}} = m C_p \ln \left( \frac{T_2}{T_1} \right)
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{gases}} = 1 \text{ kg} \times 1.005 \text{ kJ/kgK} \ln \left( \frac{550 + 273.15}{1100 + 273.15} \right)
   \]
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{gases}} = 1.005 \ln \left( \frac{823.15}{1373.15} \right) \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

2. **Change in entropy of the water**:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{m \Delta H_f}{T}
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{1 \text{ kg} \times 1858.5 \text{ kJ/kg}}{220 + 273.15} \text{ kJ/K}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{1858.5}{493.15} \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

3. **Total entropy change**:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{total}} = \Delta S_{\text{gases}} + \Delta S_{\text{water}}
   \]
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{total}} = 1.005 \ln \left( \frac{823.15}{1373.15} \right) + \frac{1858.5}{493.15} \text{ kJ/K}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{total}} = 1.005 \ln \left( \frac{823.15}{1373.15} \right) + 3.70 \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

   The numerical value is approximately:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{total}} = -0.30 \text{ kJ/K} + 3.70 \text{ kJ/K} = 3.40 \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

   The total entropy of the combined system increases by \(\boxed{3.40 \text{ kJ/K}}\).
