Flow velocity (v) = Flow rate (Q) / Cross-sectional area (A)
The cross-sectional area (A) can be calculated using the formula for the area of a circle:
A = π * (diameter/2)²
A = π * (0.1 mm / 2)²
A = π * (0.05 mm)²
A = π * 0.00025 in²

Now, convert the flow rate from cm³ min⁻¹ to cm²/s:
Q = 10 cm³ min⁻¹ * (1 cc / 1 cm³) * (1 min / 60 s)
