The standard Gibbs free energy of formation (ΔGf°) of water is given as -237.1 kJ/mol. Since the standard Gibbs free energy of formation of the elements in their standard states (H2 and O2) is zero, we can calculate the change in Gibbs free energy for the reaction as follows:

ΔG = [2 × ΔGf°(H2O)] - [2 × ΔGf°(H2) + ΔGf°(O2)]
ΔG = [2 × (-237.1 kJ/mol)] - [2 × 0 + 0]
ΔG = -474.2 kJ/mol

So, the change in Gibbs free energy for the reaction is -474.2 kJ/mol.
