1. \( \phi_1 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix} \) (synchronous motion)  
2. \( \phi_2 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{bmatrix} \) (anti-phase motion)  
3. \( \phi_3 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \end{bmatrix} \) (anti-phase motion)  

**Step 5: Orthogonality Check**  
The mode shapes are orthogonal with respect to the mass matrix \( M \):  

\[ \phi_i^T M \phi_j = 0 \quad \text{for} \quad i \neq j \]  

